WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:04.229
Before they took over TruTV and started their
search for Larry…

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.260
"Larry?

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.480
Larry?

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:07.660
Larry!"

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:12.370
...the Impractical Jokers were once once just
a regular gang of pranksters from Staten Island.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:15.740
But what did Q, Murr, Sal, and Joe do before
TV stardom?

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.490
From their beginnings in high school through
their days as the New York-based comedy troupe,

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:23.759
the Tenderloins, Here's a look at the Impractical
Jokers before all the fame.

00:00:23.759 --> 00:00:24.759
Catholic school

00:00:24.759 --> 00:00:29.740
The guys first met in a religion class at
Monsignor Farrell, an all-boys Catholic high

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.720
school in Staten Island, where they banded
together and quickly realized that the best

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.560
way to meet girls was through acting.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.880
But when they weren't acting, they were pranking.

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:42.710
In a senior year prank they called "Rice Capades",
the guys dumped ten-pound bags of rice in

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.000
the school's hallways.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.470
As Q told Fox Sports,

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.910
"Students were slipping and sliding in it
everywhere.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:48.910
We had rice fights.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:49.920
It was a blast.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.230
Took the janitorial crew weeks to get all
the rice out of the school.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.890
This put the administration in no mood for
further shenanigans.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.940
So, of course, we pushed it further later
in the year."

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:03.140
"Vermin Day" eventually earned Q detention
when he was caught putting a goldfish in a

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:04.140
toilet.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.530
Though that was tame in comparison to the
squirrels, crabs, birds, turtles, and cats

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:10.799
that were released through the school that
same day.

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:14.700
Both rice and cats would figure prominently
into their later pranks.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:18.840
"There's so many places on my body to hide
rice.

00:01:21.299 --> 00:01:22.509
Fold after fold.

00:01:22.509 --> 00:01:23.590
Crevice after crevice.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:25.810
I mean I get two boxes no problem."

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:32.799
Brian Quinn

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:37.380
Before he started his career as a professional
television jokester, Brian Quinn, better known

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:41.220
these days as Q, was a member of the New York
City Fire Department.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:47.380
After taking a leave of absence to film Impractical
Jokers, he returned to the FDNY with a $50,000

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.380
donation.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:52.030
But that didn't stop the Jokers from mercilessly
teasing him about leaving his life of heroism

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:52.750
behind.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.950
"I heard you were you were a great fireman."

00:01:56.219 --> 00:01:58.679
"No, I'm an actor on television."

00:01:58.679 --> 00:02:02.799
As a kid, he was also obsessed with Star Wars
and forced his parents to take him to see

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:05.609
Return of the Jedi in theaters four times.

00:02:05.609 --> 00:02:08.500
Q still maintains his collection of Star Wars
toys today.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.420
At one point, Q was engaged, but it didn't
go well.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:12.660
"Will you marry me?"

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.920
"Okay, but two weeks before the wedding I'm
gonna dump you and marry a cop."

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.220
"That's actually what happened to Q!"

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:25.720
Q was almost a regular cast member of Comic
Book Men, having served as one of Kevin Smith's

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:30.880
first assistants at the View Askew offices,
and a host of the Tell 'Em Steve Dave podcast.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:35.300
Fortunately for viewers, Q's contract with
TruTV made him stick with the Jokers.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:39.250
Q was a fan of the Tenderloins before he was
formally accepted as a part of their crew

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:41.500
as a replacement for a departing member.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:45.740
When the guys gave him an opportunity to perform
with them, comedic magic was made.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.140
"Go, go, go, go, go!"

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.810
"Uh, I'm gonna kill every one of ya.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:52.910
You're all dead."

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:54.360
James Murray

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.620
As a kid, James Murray loved pro wrestling
and baseball.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:02.280
His fondest childhood sports memory was watching
Bobby "The Brain" Heenan get his teeth smashed

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:07.770
out by Hulk Hogan, followed years later seeing
Roger Clemens throw a broken bat at Mike Piazza,

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.210
all live and in person.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:13.270
You probably know all about Murr's vocal talents
from the show…

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:14.920
"Geronimo!"

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.210
(high-pitched screams)

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:22.091
… but he also starred in multiple musicals
throughout his attendance at Georgetown, and

00:03:22.091 --> 00:03:25.150
eventually graduated with a BA in English.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:29.700
As fans may already know, Murr's father was
going to buy him a Ford Taurus as a graduation

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:34.540
gift, but Murr opted for the $30,000 cash
instead so that he could finish a film project,

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.950
a comedy about a modern teenaged Jesus.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.410
The rest is TV history.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:40.650
"Enjoy the next 50 minutes of your life."

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:48.720
"I've tried to take into account that you
were young, but Orson Welles was in his twenties

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.380
when he made Citizen Kane, what's your excuse?"

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:55.570
The ambidextrous James Murray made a brief
appearance in the Howard Stern movie, Private

00:03:55.570 --> 00:04:00.510
Parts, as an extra, and worked as a TV producer
on shows like Say Yes to the Dress before

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.320
humiliating himself on television.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.010
He maintains a simple life philosophy.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:08.940
"Here's my opinion: life's too short not to
put everything in your mouth twice.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:10.130
Once to see if you like it.

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:12.210
Second time to see if you were right about
it the first time."

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.850
Salvatore Vulcano

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:18.699
As a kid, Sal enjoyed playing basketball,
football and hockey, and later graduated from

00:04:18.699 --> 00:04:21.310
St. John's University with a degree in finance.

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:25.979
While studying at St. John's, Sal starred
in a comedic mockumentary video series titled

00:04:25.979 --> 00:04:27.610
Superdude &amp; Friend.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:31.889
Sal keeps his personal life relatively private,
which is often a subject of antagonism among

00:04:31.889 --> 00:04:32.889
his friends.

00:04:32.889 --> 00:04:36.250
"Let's look into Sal's personal life!

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:39.680
Let's look into Sal's personal life!"

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:44.130
Before engaging in a life of self-humiliation,
Sal claims that his most embarrassing moment

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:49.000
was when his babysitter saw him naked when
he was five, according to a Reddit AMA.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:53.930
At one point in his early Jokers career, Sal
was part owner of The Full Cup in Staten Island,

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.360
though he's since left the business.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:59.840
In addition to his humiliating Jaden Smith
tattoo, his ink also includes song lyrics

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.470
dedicated to a deceased friend.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:05.740
And, as Murr once revealed, Sal cannot sleep
without a sleep apnea machine.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:10.300
In his spare time, Sal is known to take womens'
pants hostage and send creepy photos to their

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.479
real owners.

00:05:11.479 --> 00:05:12.479
Joseph Gatto

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:16.419
"And now, the moment you've all been waiting
for…"

00:05:16.419 --> 00:05:17.889
"This is ridiculous.

00:05:17.889 --> 00:05:19.370
This is insane."

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:23.039
After attending high school with the rest
of the guys, Joe got his undergraduate degree

00:05:23.039 --> 00:05:25.509
in accounting from LIU Post.

00:05:25.509 --> 00:05:30.090
Just before going full-time Joker, Joe worked
as a personal shopper in a baby store, and

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:32.800
today, he's the only Joker who's married and
has a kid.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:36.650
In addition to pranks, Gatto's other true
passion is food; he's recalled how, growing

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:41.249
up in a large Italian family, there was always
an open-door policy for meals, which regularly

00:05:41.249 --> 00:05:42.550
included guests.

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:47.060
Gatto's food-fueled upbringing often translates
into his jokes and pranks today.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:51.909
And despite keeping his private life relatively
private, Joe's wife has made regular appearances

00:05:51.909 --> 00:05:52.909
on the show.

00:05:52.909 --> 00:05:54.569
"Obviously, you know this is game.

00:05:54.569 --> 00:05:55.630
I have to kiss her.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:56.630
It means nothing."

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:59.599
"You can kiss her if you want to sleep on
the couch tonight."

00:05:59.599 --> 00:06:01.479
Getting the Gang Back Together

00:06:01.479 --> 00:06:06.139
The guys all went their separate ways, until
one day Murr ran into Sal on the ferry, where

00:06:06.139 --> 00:06:10.560
the two reminisced about their former improv
days, inspiring them to get the group together.

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:14.930
From there, the guys practiced their sketches
together in Joe's mom's basement for six years.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:19.050
At the time, they all had day jobs, but were
having so much fun performing for virtually

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:22.849
no one that they decided to take their underground
troupe to the next level.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:26.949
In 1999, they formed "The Tenderloins", because
the word 'tenderloin' was something Sal was

00:06:26.949 --> 00:06:29.830
uncomfortable saying in front of a large group
of people.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:31.949
"Who wants a…"

00:06:31.949 --> 00:06:34.069
"Oh god he's gonna say it to him.

00:06:34.069 --> 00:06:34.589
He has to."

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:39.800
"Who wants a…"

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:40.810
Time Thugs

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:45.300
The Impractical Jokers got their first shot
at stardom after winning $100,000 on It's

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:50.520
Your Show on NBC, a video submission contest
hosted by Carson Daly, with a comedy clip

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:52.039
titled "Time Thugs."

00:06:52.039 --> 00:06:57.419
"Our skilled goons will travel back through
the time stream to completely destroy anyone

00:06:57.419 --> 00:06:59.169
who might've steered your life wrong."

00:06:59.169 --> 00:07:03.379
The newfound fame and cash inspired the guys
to take a stab at tv, filming a pilot for

00:07:03.379 --> 00:07:05.580
Spike TV called Mission Uncomfortable.

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:10.129
Spike passed on the project, but the undaunted
Tenderloins began their evolution into television's

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:14.360
Impractical Jokers, piling up a series of
early gigs that even included opening for

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.240
Imagine Dragons — as a joke, of course.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.949
"We are very happy to be here..."

00:07:18.949 --> 00:07:20.840
"Opening for Imagination Dragons."

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.900
"Opening for the Imagination Dragons."

00:07:26.059 --> 00:07:27.089
Thanks for watching!

00:07:27.089 --> 00:07:29.680
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:31.849
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

